1. Where does React put all of the elements I create in JSX when I 
   call `root.render()`?
The root element, determined by whichever element or ID you declare as root

2. What would show up in my console if I were to run this line of code:
```
console.log(<h1>Hello world!</h1>)
```
Syntax error

3. What's wrong with this code:
```
root.render(
    <h1>Hi there</h1>
    <p>This is my website!</p>
)
```
No parent element

4. What does it mean for something to be "declarative" instead of "imperative"?
Declarative is what React is, give an instruction and itll be done with parameters set beforehand, imperative means you need to describe each step precisely

5. What does it mean for something to be "composable"?
You can make all kinds of personal changes and compositions to the system.